          array (
            0 => 
            array (
              'id' => 'css_input',
              'label' => 'Enter CSS Code',
              'type' => 'textarea',
              'default' => '/* Example CSS */
.header {
  color: #333;
  margin: 10px;
}',
              'placeholder' => 'Paste your CSS here...',
            ),
          ),
        ),
        'engine_formula' => 'css_compressor',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>Optimize Your Site Performance with the CSS Compressor</h2><p>In the competitive world of web development, every kilobyte counts. The <strong>CSS Compressor</strong> is a high-end "webmaster tool" designed to strip away unnecessary characters from your style sheets without altering their functionality. By removing whitespace, comments, and line breaks, you can reduce file sizes by up to 30%, leading to faster "page load times" and improved "SEO scores."</p><h3>Why Minify Your CSS?</h3><p>Browsers don\'t need human-readable formatting to interpret CSS. While indentation and comments are helpful for developers, they represent redundant data for the end-user. Minification is a "DevOps-grade" practice that ensures your production assets are as lean as possible. Faster sites provide a better user experience, lower bounce rates, and are favored by Google\'s Core Web Vitals algorithms.</p><h3>How the Logic Works</h3><p>Our compressor uses advanced regex patterns to:<ul><li>Remove all CSS comments (/* ... */].</li><li>Strip trailing semicolons before closing braces.</li><li>Collapse multiple spaces and newlines into a single character.</li><li>Remove spaces around punctuation like colons and braces.</li></ul>The result is a single-line "minified" version of your code that the browser can parse instantly.</p><h3>Features of Our Dashboard</h3><ul><li><strong>Before vs After Comparison:</strong> See exactly how many bytes you saved.</li><li><strong>Compression Percentage:</strong> Track the efficiency of the minification.</li><li><strong>Enhanced Output Tabs:</strong> Switch between "Raw" and "Clean" views or download the result directly.</li></ul><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q: Will this break my site?</strong><br>A: No. Our logic only removes non-functional whitespace and comments. The CSS structure remains intact.</p><p><strong>Q: Should I keep my original CSS?</strong><br>A: Yes! Always keep a "development" version that is readable. Only use the compressed version for "production" environments.</p>',
