      'content' => '<h2>Clean Up Your Data with the HTML to Text Converter</h2><p>Sometimes, raw code is just noise. Whether you are building an email preview, performing "SEO competitive analysis," or training an AI model, you often need the <strong>Clean Text</strong> without the tags. The HTML to Text Converter is a professional "SEO tool" and data utility that strips away HTML elements while attempting to preserve the natural flow of the document. This process is crucial for converting complex web pages into readable snippets or logs.</p><h3>Preserving Structure During Extraction</h3><p>Unlike simple "strip_tags" functions, our converter handles common formatting rules:<ul><li><strong>Line Breaks:</strong> Converts <code>&lt;br&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> tags into logical newlines.</li><li><strong>Lists:</strong> Adds bullets to <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> items for readability.</li><li><strong>Headings:</strong> Capitalizes or separates <code>&lt;h1-h6&gt;</code> tags to maintain hierarchy.</li><li><strong>Whiepsace:</strong> Collapses redundant spaces while keeping paragraph spacing.</li></ul>This "standardized" approach ensures that your output is not just a block of text, but a formatted <strong>Clean Version</strong> of the original content.</p><h3>SEO and Accessibility Value</h3><p>Converting HTML to text allows you to see your content exactly how a screen reader or a basic search engine crawler might perceive it. By reviewing the text-only version, you can detect keyword stuffing or missing information that might be buried in the code. This is an essential part of an "SEO score" audit for any high-end website architecture.</p><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q: Does this preserve links?</strong><br>A: Yes, it can be configured to keep the URL next to the link text for reference.</p><p><strong>Q: Can it handle JavaScript?</strong><br>A: It strips <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> tags entirely to focus on the visible content.</p>',
