        'engine_formula' => 'favicon_generator',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>Perfect Your Branding with the Favicon Generator</h2><p>The <strong>Favicon</strong> is the tiny icon that represents your website in browser tabs, bookmarks, and mobile home screens. While small, it is a massive part of your site\'s professional "first impression." The Favicon Generator is a "webmaster tool" that allows you to preview your icon in a real-world browser tab environment before you deploy it to production. This "UX-first" approach ensures your brand is recognizable even when a user has dozens of tabs open.</p><h3>Visualizing the User Experience</h3><p>Most designers create favicons at large sizes, but they often lose clarity when scaled down to the standard 16x16 or 32x32 pixels. Our dashboard provides a <strong>High-Fidelity Tab Mockup</strong>, allowing you to see how your icon interacts with typical browser colors and tab titles. This is a crucial step in "interactive-ready" design, ensuring that your colors pop and your logo is legible at miniature scale.</p><h3>Technical Requirements for Modern Favicons</h3><p>Years ago, a simple <code>favicon.ico</code> was enough. Today, webmasters must handle Apple Touch Icons, Android manifest icons, and SVG favicons for dark mode support. Our tool provides a <strong>Validated Code Snippet</strong> that you can paste into your <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> to ensure your icon works across all devices, including iPhones and high-res desktops. This standardized approach is essential for modern "SEO systems design."</p><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q: Which format is best?</strong><br>A: SVG is best for modern browsers because it scales perfectly and supports dark mode. Use a 32x32 PNG for legacy compatibility.</p><p><strong>Q: Why is my favicon not updating?</strong><br>A: Most browsers cache favicons aggressively. You may need to visit <code>yoursite.com/favicon.ico</code> and force-refresh the page.</p>',
