      'content' => '<h2>Beyond the Standard GCD</h2><p>The <strong>Extended Euclidean Algorithm</strong> is an expansion of the classic algorithm for finding the greatest common divisor (GCD] of two integers. While the basic algorithm only gives you the GCD, the extended version also finds the "BÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â©zout coefficients" <strong>x</strong> and <strong>y</strong> such that: <strong>ax + by = gcd(a, b]</strong>. This specific calculation is a cornerstone of advanced mathematics and cryptography. Our Extended Euclidean Calculator provides a full step-by-step breakdown of the process.</p><h3>Solving Linear Diophantine Equations</h3><p>The relationship ax + by = d is known as a "Linear Diophantine Equation." The extended algorithm is the primary method for solving these equations, which appear in "Resource Allocation" and "Inventory Management" problems where variables must be integers. It also allows you to find the <strong>Modular Multiplicative Inverse</strong>, which is required whenever you need to "divide" in modular arithmetic (e.g., in encryption protocols].</p><h3>Applications in Computer Science</h3><p>In <strong>Cryptography</strong>, the extended algorithm is used to find the modular inverse during the generation of RSA keys. It is also used in the <strong>Chinese Remainder Theorem</strong> to solve systems of congruences. Because it works with integers and is extremely fast, it is a fundamental algorithm for competitive programming and secure systems engineering. Our calculator helps you visualize how the quotients and remainders are "back-substituted" to arrive at the final coefficients.</p><h3>How to Use the Extended Solver</h3><p>Enter your two integers, a and b. The tool will calculate the GCD and the values for x and y. You will also see a detailed "Work Table" showing the forward steps (division] and backward steps (substitution] of the algorithm. It is an essential tool for "Number Theory" students and "Cybersecurity" professionals. solve complex modular problems with our professional Extended Euclidean Algorithm Calculator.</p>',
