        By rearranging this formula, we can solve for any unknown factor as long as the other three are known. Our calculator performs these algebraic rearrangements automatically.</p><h3>Applications in Archeology and Medicine</h3><p>In <strong>Archeology</strong>, half-life is the basis of "Carbon-14 Dating," allowing scientists to determine the age of organic materials by measuring the remaining radioactive carbon. In <strong>Medicine</strong>, it helps pharmacists determine how often a patient should take a pill based on the "Biological Half-Life" of the active ingredient. In <strong>Environmental Science</strong>, it measures the "Persistence" of pollutants in soil and water. Understanding half-life is critical for safety and accurate timing in scientific fields.</p><h3>Using the Solver Utility</h3><p>Select which variable you want to find (e.g., "Find Remaining Amount"]. Enter the known values for the other fields. The tool will provide the result along with a "Decay Steps" visualization showing the quantity after each successive half-life period. It also provides the "Decay Constant" (ÃƒÅ½Ã‚Â»], which is the continuous rate equivalent. accurately model scientific decay with our professional Half-Life Calculator.</p>',
