        ),
        'engine_formula' => 'set_theory_calc',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>The Foundations of Set Theory</h2><p>In "Mathematical Logic" and "Discrete Mathematics," <strong>Set Theory</strong> is the study of collections of objects. Understanding how different groups (sets] overlap or differ is essential for information indexing, database design, and statistical analysis. Our Set Theory Calculator allows you to input two collections and instantly see all of their logical relationships. It handles numbers, letters, and words with ease.</p><h3>Core Set Operations Explained</h3><p>Our tool calculates the following standard operations:
        - <strong>Union (A ÃƒÂ¢Ã‹â€ Ã‚Âª B]:</strong> All unique elements that are in either Set A, Set B, or both.
        - <strong>Intersection (A ÃƒÂ¢Ã‹â€ Ã‚Â© B]:</strong> Only the elements that are common to both sets.
        - <strong>Relative Complement (A - B]:</strong> Elements in A that are NOT in B.
        - <strong>Symmetric Difference:</strong> Elements that are in either A or B, but not both.
        Each operation provides a distinct "View" of your data, helping you identify unique items versus shared dependencies.</p><h3>Applications in Computer Science and Data</h3><p>Set theory is the underlying logic for <strong>SQL Joins</strong> in database management; "INNER JOIN" is an intersection, while "LEFT JOIN" is related to the union. In <strong>Search Engines</strong>, Boolean operators (AND, OR, NOT] are direct applications of set theory. In <strong>Software Engineering</strong>, using "Sets" instead of lists can dramatically improve performance when checking for the existence of an item. If you are managing data, you are using set theory.</p><h3>How to Use the set Theory Tool</h3><p>Enter your items for Set A and Set B, separated by commas. The calculator will provide a "Venn Comparison" of the sets and a detailed list of results for each operation. It also calculates the "Cardinality" (the size] of each set and tells you if one set is a <strong>Subset</strong> of the other. Whether you are studying for a "Logic" exam or cleaning a dataset, our Set Theory Calculator is a reliable and accurate resource. Master the relationships of data with our professional Set Theory Calculator.</p>',
    ),
    'stirling-numbers-calculator' => 
