        'engine_formula' => 'venn_generator',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>Visualizing Logic with Venn Diagrams</h2><p>A <strong>Venn Diagram</strong> is a visual representation of the logical relationships between a set of items. Invented by John Venn in the 1880s, it uses overlapping circles to show where different groups share common traits. While a 2-set diagram is simple, a <strong>3-Set Venn Diagram</strong> is far more powerful, identifying seven distinct regions of overlap and uniqueness. Our Venn Diagram Generator is a professional utility that makes these complex intersections clear and easy to understand.</p><h3>The Anatomy of a 3-Set Venn</h3><p>When three circles overlap, they create:
        - <strong>3 Exclusive Regions:</strong> Items that belong only to Set A, Set B, or Set C.
        - <strong>3 Primary Intersections:</strong> Items that belong to exactly two sets (AÃƒÂ¢Ã‹â€ Ã‚Â©B, BÃƒÂ¢Ã‹â€ Ã‚Â©C, and AÃƒÂ¢Ã‹â€ Ã‚Â©C].
        - <strong>1 Inner Core:</strong> Items that belong to all three sets (AÃƒÂ¢Ã‹â€ Ã‚Â©BÃƒÂ¢Ã‹â€ Ã‚Â©C].
        Our generator allows you to label each set and assign values to each region, providing a perfect illustration for "Statistical Reports" or "Business Presentations."</p><h3>Applications in Marketing and Science</h3><p>In <strong>Business Strategy</strong>, Venn diagrams are used to find the "Sweet Spot" where customer needs, market trends, and company capabilities overlap. In <strong>Biology</strong>, they visualize shared genes between three different species. In <strong>Software Engineering</strong>, they help developers understand complex logic conditions that involve three different variables. If you need to "Visualize a Comparison," the Venn diagram is the most recognized and effective tool available.</p><h3>How to Use the Generator</h3><p>Customize the labels for your three sets. Then, enter the numeric values for each region (or leave them at 1 for a simple structural diagram]. The tool will generate a "High-Resolution SVG" diagram that is clear and proportional. You can use this for academic posters, pitch decks, or simply to clarify your own thinking about a complex problem. Simplify your logical comparisons with our professional 3-Set Venn Diagram Generator.</p>',
    ),
