        'engine_formula' => 'median_calc',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>The Median: Finding the True Center of a Data Set</h2>
<p>The <strong>median</strong> is the value separating the higher half from the lower half of a data sample, a population, or a probability distribution. For a data set, it may be thought of as the "middle" value. In a sorted list of numbers, the median is the number at the center. It is a critical measure of central tendency, particularly when dealing with data that is unevenly distributed or contains "flier" values.</p>
<h3>Difference Between Odd and Even Data Sets</h3>
<p>The calculation method changes slightly based on count:
- <strong>Odd Number of Values:</strong> The median is simply the middle number. In {1, 3, 5}, the median is 3.
- <strong>Even Number of Values:</strong> The median is the arithmetic average of the two middle numbers. In {1, 2, 4, 8}, the middle numbers are 2 and 4, so the median is (2+4]/2 = 3.
Our calculator handles these rules automatically, ensuring you never have to worry about the index math yourself.</p>
<h3>Why the Median is More "Honest" Than the Mean</h3>
<p>The median\'s greatest strength is that it is <strong>robust to outliers</strong>. Imagine a room of 10 people earning $40,000. If one billionaire walks in, the "Average" (Mean] income jumps to millions of dollars, giving a false impression of everyone\'s wealth. However, the <strong>Median</strong> remains $40,000. This is why the median is the legally and statistically preferred way to report <strong>household income, real estate prices, and net worth</strong> ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â it represents the "real" experience of the person in the middle.</p>
<h3>When to Choose the Median</h3>
<p>You should use the median whenever your data is <strong>skewed</strong>. A distribution is skewed if most of the values are bunched up on one side with a "tail" stretching out to the other. In these cases, the mean is "pulled" toward the tail, while the median stays centered among the bulk of the population. Whether you are analyzing salary surveys, housing markets, or test scores, our Median Calculator provides a stable, reliable center-point for your findings.</p>',
