In fields like electrical engineering and signal processing, these identities are used to analyze alternating currents and harmonize frequencies. If an engineer needs to combine two sine waves with different phases, the Sum-to-Product identities are the standard way to find the resulting wave. Our calculator provides the precision needed for these technical applications, with rounding support for up to 10 decimal places. This ensures that even small rounding errors don\'t obscure the fact that the two sides of the identity are mathematically identical.

