              'default' => '1, 1',
              'placeholder' => 'e.g., 0.5, 0.5',
            ),
          ),
        ),
        'engine_formula' => 'convolution_calc',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>What is Convolution?</h2><p>In digital signal processing and mathematics, <strong>Convolution</strong> is an operation on two functions that produces a third function expressing how the shape of one is modified by the other. For discrete sequences, it is the fundamental way to calculate the output of a <strong>Linear Time-Invariant (LTI] System</strong>. Our Convolution Calculator provides the full output sequence (y[n]] and the step-by-step sliding-window calculation.</p><h3>The Convolution Formula</h3><p>For two discrete sequences x[n] and h[n], the convolution (y[n]] is defined as:<br><strong>y[n] = ÃƒÅ½Ã‚Â£ x[k] * h[n - k]</strong><br>As h[n-k] "slides" across x[k], the overlapping terms are multiplied and summed. This process is used to model <strong>Filters</strong>, <strong>Echoes</strong>, and <strong>System Responses</strong> in everything from audio engineering to image processing. Our tool handles sequences of any length with scientific accuracy.</p><h3>Applications in Engineering and Data</h3><p>Convolution is the backbone of <strong>CNNs (Convolutional Neural Networks]</strong> in Artificial Intelligence, where filters slide across pixel data to identify features like edges and textures. In <strong>Audio Engineering</strong>, convolution is used for "Reverb Modeling," allowing a dry signal to sound as if it were played in a specific physical space. In <strong>Probability</strong>, the convolution of two probability distributions gives the distribution of the sum of two independent random variables.</p><h3>Using the Convolution Solver</h3><p>Enter your two sequences separated by commas. The calculator will provide the "Output Sequence," the "Total Energy" of the result, and a step-by-step table showing the "Slide and Multiply" process. You will also see a visual "Signal Plot" of the input and output waves. This utility is an essential resource for students of electrical engineering and data science. Master the math of signals with our professional Convolution Calculator.</p>',
    ),
    'curvature-calculator' => 
