          ),
        ),
        'engine_formula' => 'curvature_calc',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>The Geometry of Curvature</h2><p>In mathematics, <strong>Curvature</strong> (denoted by the Greek letter kappa, ÃƒÅ½Ã‚Âº] is a measure of how quickly a curve changes direction at a given point. For a flat line, the curvature is zero. For a circle, the curvature is constant and equal to the reciprocal of the radius (1/R]. Our Curvature Calculator uses the standard calculus formula to find this metric for any twice-differentiable function, providing insights into the "Sharpness" of mathematical turns.</p><h3>The Curvature Formula</h3><p>For a function y = f(x], the curvature is defined as:<br><strong>ÃƒÅ½Ã‚Âº = |f"(x]| / (1 + (f\'(x]]Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â²]Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â³/Ãƒâ€šÃ‚Â²</strong><br>Where <strong>f\'(x]</strong> is the first derivative (slope] and <strong>f"(x]</strong> is the second derivative (rate of change of slope]. This formula tells us that curvature is high when the second derivative is large and the slope is small. Our tool performs numerical differentiation to find these values with high precision, mapping the exact "Turn Rate" of your curve.</p><h3>Use Cases in Physics and Engineering</h3><p>In <strong>Physics</strong>, curvature is used to calculate "Centripetal Acceleration" for objects moving along curved paths (a = vÃƒâ€šÃ‚Â²ÃƒÅ½Ã‚Âº]. In <strong>Civil Engineering</strong>, it is used to design safe "Highway Curves" and railway tracks to ensure vehicles don\'t experience excessive lateral forces. In <strong>Optics</strong>, the curvature of a lens determines its focal length and "Refractive Power." Understanding curvature is essential for anyone designing motion or light paths in the physical world.</p><h3>How to Use the Curvature Tool</h3><p>Input your function and the x-coordinate where you want to measure. The calculator will provide the "Curvature (ÃƒÅ½Ã‚Âº]," the "Radius of Curvature (R = 1/ÃƒÅ½Ã‚Âº]," and the "Center of Curvature" coordinates. You will also see a visual representation of the <strong>Osculating Circle</strong>ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âthe circle that best fits the curve at that specific point. It is an advanced resource for calculus and differential geometry. Measure the turns of math with our professional Curvature Calculator.</p>',
    ),
    'fourier-series-coefficients' => 
    array (
      'title' => 'Fourier Series Coefficients Calculator - a0, an, bn Tool',
      'h1' => 'Fourier Series Coefficients Calculator',
      'subtitle' => 'Calculate coefficients for periodic function decomposition.',
