        'engine_formula' => 'html_beautifier_calc',
        'button_text' => 'Beautify HTML',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>Everything You Need to Know About HTML Beautifier</h2>
<p>In the high-stakes world of modern web development, the difference between a successful project and a maintenance nightmare often lies in the quality of the source code. The <strong>HTML Beautifier</strong> is a precision-engineered utility designed to transform fragmented, minified, or inconsistently formatted HTML markup into a clean, hierarchical, and professional-grade document structure. Whether you are dealing with "Spaghetti Code" inherited from a legacy project or trying to make sense of a compressed third-party script, this tool provides the structural clarity required for deep technical analysis. By applying a deterministic indentation logicÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âbased on nested tag hierarchiesÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âthe Beautifier ensures that every opening and closing tag is perfectly aligned, allowing developers to spot missing tags and architectural flaws in seconds rather than hours.</p>

<h3>The Mechanics of Code Indentation and Semantic Parsing</h3>
<p>The logic driving our HTML Beautifier goes far beyond a simple "find and replace" operation. It utilizes a recursive parsing engine that treats your HTML as a "Document Object Tree." When you paste your code into the analyzer, the engine first identifies the relationship between parent and child elements. It then applies a consistent, user-friendly indentation of two spaces per nesting level. This "Structural Isolation" approach is critical for accessibility and performance; well-formatted code is easier for screen readers to navigate and for search engine crawlers to index correctly. Our tool also handles self-closing tags (like &lt;img&gt; or &lt;br&gt;] with extreme care, ensuring they don\'t break the indentation chain for subsequent elements. This level of technical precision makes it an essential "Primitive" in any developer\'s toolkit, bridging the gap between raw functional code and premium, maintainable engineering.</p>

<h3>Common Use Cases and Professional Developer Workflows</h3>
<p>Professional front-end engineers utilize HTML beautifiers primarily for "Code Auditing" and "Refactoring." When a website layout breaks, the first step is always to verify the tag nesting. By running the code through our Beautifier, you can immediately identify "Tag Mismatch Errors" that are nearly impossible to see in a single-line minified file. Beyond debugging, this tool is indispensable for "Learning and Documentation." If you find a brilliant piece of UI on a website and want to understand how it was built, you can copy the source and use our tool to deconstruct the architecture. It is also a staple for teams that use "Git" or other version control systems; by beautifying code before a commit, you ensure that "Diffs" are clean and meaningful, preventing "Whitespace Noise" from cluttering your project history. Furthermore, content creators who work with CMS platforms use it to clean up the "Dirty HTML" often generated by visual editors.</p>

<h3>Technical Precision and Data Privacy Integrity</h3>
<p>At ToolsHub, we understand that your source code is your intellectual property. That is why our HTML Beautifier is built on a "Local-First" architecture. All parsing and formatting operations occur directly within your browser\'s memory; your code is never transmitted to our servers or stored in any external database. This makes it a secure choice for developers working on proprietary enterprise software or sensitive personal projects. The tool is optimized for speed, capable of formatting thousands of lines of markup in milliseconds without any browser lag. The output is delivered in a high-visibility, copy-ready format, ensuring that you can move your refined code back into your IDE (like VS Code or Sublime Text] instantly. Whether you are a student learning the ropes of web development or a seasoned Senior Architect, our HTML Beautifier provides the reliability, speed, and professional finish you need to work with total confidence.</p>
<h3>Key Benefits of Our Setup</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Lightning Fast:</strong> Runs purely client-side without any backend delay.</li><li><strong>Data Privacy:</strong> No inputs or outputs are logged. Everything lives in your browser.</li><li><strong>Multi-Format:</strong> View the results in raw, clean, or structured views.</li></ul>',
    ),
    'html-to-markdown' => 
    array (
      'title' => 'HTML to Markdown - Instant Content Converter',
      'h1' => 'HTML to Markdown Converter',
      'subtitle' => 'Cleanly translate web markup into lightweight Markdown syntax.',
