<p>Our Beautifier doesn\'t just add random spaces; it follows a strict "Syntax-Aware" logic that respects the unique rules of CSS and JavaScript. For CSS, the engine identifies selector blocks and property-value pairs, ensuring each rule is on its own line and indented correctly relative to the opening brace. For JavaScript, it handles the complex nesting of functions, loops, and object literals. The logic includes a "Breathing Room" algorithm that ensures semicolons are followed by a new line and that trailing spaces are eliminated. This level of technical precision prevents "Syntax Noise" and allows the developer to focus on the logical flow of the code. By turning "Minified Spaghetti" into "Structured Proof-of-Concept" code, we provide a "No-Code" way to perform what would otherwise require a specialized IDE plugin or a heavy NPM package like Prettier or JS-Beautify.</p>

<h3>Common Use Cases and Professional Developer Workflows</h3>
