              'default' => 'http://google.com',
              'placeholder' => 'Enter URL to check...',
            ),
          ),
        ),
        'engine_formula' => 'redirect_checker',
        'button_text' => 'Check Redirect Path',
      ),
      'content' => '<h2>Mastering Website Migration with the Redirect Checker</h2><p>In the high-stakes landscape of "Search Engine Optimization (SEO]" and "Domain Infrastructure," the **Redirect Checker** is a critical "Surgical Utility." Every time a URL moves, it creates a potential point of failure. A 301 redirect that hops through four different domains before reaching its destination isn\'t just slowÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âit\'s an "SEO Leak." Our tool provides a definitive, "Zero-Placeholder Audit" of any URL path, following the "HTTP Header Stream" until the final status is reached. Whether you are a "Senior SEO Architect" diagnosing "Link Equity Loss," a "DevOps Professional" verifying "Nginx Rewrite Rules," or a "Brand Manager" ensuring "Campaign URL Integrity," our tool delivers the "Technical Resolution" required for absolute site health.</p><h3>The Science of HTTP Hops and Status Code Resolution</h3><p>The core logic of our Redirect Engine is built on "Synchronized Header Parsing." Unlike simple browser-based checks that can be influenced by "Local Cache" or "Browser Extensions," our checker makes a direct server-side request. It identifies and categorizes every response in the chain: **301 (Permanent], 302 (Found], 307 (Temporary], and 308 (Permanent Redirect]**. The engine calculates the **Hop Count** and the **Total Latency** of the journey, highlighting "Redirect Loops" that would otherwise crash a crawler or a user browser. This level of technical precision is essential for "Enterprise Site Migrations" where thousands of legacy URLs must be correctly mapped to new canonical destinations. The output card features a "Structured Chain Table" and a highlighted **Final Destination URL** for immediate verification.</p><h3>Use Cases for Technical SEOs, Security Analysts, and Affiliate Marketers</h3><p>Professional "Technical SEO Auditors" utilize the Redirect Checker to ensure that "Crawl Budget" is not wasted on redundant intermediate hops. "Cybersecurity Researchers" use it to identify "Malicious URL Cloaking" where a seemingly benign link redirects through a series of "Phishing Jump-Sites." "Affiliate Marketers" use the tool to verify that their "Tracking Pixels" and "Attribution Parameters" survive the journey through various affiliate networks. "Marketing Automation Leads" use it to test "Email Tracking Links" before deployment, ensuring that customers aren\'t greeted with a 404 error. By providing a "Direct Path Visualization," the tool acts as a "Trust Factor" for your digital asset management.</p><h3>Why Eliminating Redirect Chains is a Core Web Vital</h3><p>Every "HTTP Hop" adds significant milliseconds to the "TTFB (Time to First Byte]." For mobile users on "3G or 4G Networks," a single extra redirect can add up to 500ms of lag. By identifying and "Flattening" these chains, you directly improve your site\'s performance and "User Experience Score." Google explicitly states that while they follow multiple redirects, they prefer a 1:1 relationship for maximum indexing efficiency. Our tool helps you find these hidden "Profit Killers" and resolve them before they impact your rankings.</p><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q: What is a redirect loop?</strong><br>A: A loop occurs when URL A points to URL B, and URL B points back to URL A, causing the request to never finish.ÃƒÂ¦Ã‹â€ Ã¢â‚¬ËœÃƒÂ¤Ã‚Â»Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ§Ã…Â¡Ã¢â‚¬Å¾ÃƒÂ¥Ã‚Â·Ã‚Â¥ÃƒÂ¥Ã¢â‚¬Â¦Ã‚Â· detects this automatically.</p><p><strong>Q: Can I check HTTPS redirects?</strong><br>A: Yes, our engine fully supports SSL/TLS handshakes and validates the security status of each hop.</p><p><strong>Q: Is my search history private?</strong><br>A: Yes, all checks are processed through an encrypted backend and no URL logs are permanently stored on our infrastructure.</p>',
    ),
    'robots-txt-generator' => 
    array (
      'title' => 'Robots.txt Generator - Search Crawler Rules Tool',
      'h1' => 'Robots.txt Rule Generator',
      'subtitle' => 'Create a perfectly formatted robots.txt file to control search engine crawlers.',
      'description' => 'A professional SEO utility to manage your site\'s crawlability with custom Allow/Disallow rules.',
      'icon' => 'fas fa-robot',
      'category' => 'webmaster',
      'type' => 'interactive',
      'processor' => 'interactive',
